Assets
======

king-logo.png
  The Klondike splash/logo artwork. Shown on the startup splash and the win
  banner.

fonts/
  ui.ttf / ui-bold.ttf — Atkinson Hyperlegible, a highly legible open font by the
  Braille Institute, used for all GUI text (crisp at high DPI). Licensed under the
  SIL Open Font License 1.1; the full license text is in `fonts/OFL.txt`. The GUI
  falls back to macroquad's built-in font if these are absent.

cards/
  Card face sprites and a back, named by rank + suit code, e.g. `AS.png`
  (Ace of Spades), `10H.png` (Ten of Hearts), `KD.png`, `back.png`. Suit codes:
  C = Clubs, D = Diamonds, H = Hearts, S = Spades; ranks use A, 2..10, J, Q, K.

  Source: the public-domain playing-card deck from Wikimedia Commons
  "Public domain playing cards"
  (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Public_domain_playing_cards),
  obtained via the GitHub mirror hayeah/playing-cards-assets
  (https://github.com/hayeah/playing-cards-assets), then renamed to the
  rank+suit-code scheme above. Public domain; no attribution required, cited
  here for provenance.

  These sprites are not strictly required: if the `cards/` files are absent the
  GUI falls back to drawing cards procedurally (rank + suit letter on a card
  shape), so the game remains playable.

cards-svg/
  The vector source deck, named `RANKSUIT.svg` (e.g. `AS.svg`, `10H.svg`). This
  is the "Byron Knoll" style public-domain SVG playing-card deck from Wikimedia
  Commons (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:SVG_playing_cards),
  renamed to the rank+suit-code scheme. Public domain; cited here for provenance.
  Used only at build time to generate `cards-mobile/` (below); not loaded at runtime.

cards-mobile/
  A higher-legibility card set for small/touch screens, using the same
  rank+suit-code filenames as `cards/`. Each card shows a large rank + suit on
  one row above a large, centered card body, so the index stays readable when
  cards are small or only their top strip shows in a tableau fan.

  Generated from the vector `cards-svg/` deck by `tools/build_mobile_cards.py`,
  which classifies each card's corner rank, corner pip, and body by vector
  bounding box and recomposes them into the mobile layout, rendering each region
  from vectors (crisp at any size). Build-time only; see `tools/requirements.txt`
  for the Python dependencies. Regenerate with:

    python3 tools/build_mobile_cards.py            # assets/cards-svg -> assets/cards-mobile

  Also optional: the GUI prefers this set on mobile and falls back to `cards/`
  (then to procedural cards) when it is absent.
